{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":".github/workflows/ci.yml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835071Z","id":"b0f1d8ab693a9733f308ebd6cccae0068f42363f9bcf97ecb0d724b404fa7bc0","body":{"detail":"CI's worker job runs scripts/check-wasm.sh and just worker-test natively, outside scripts/bazel-test.sh --ci, so just ci stays Bazel-only and makes no target/ or node_modules in a worktree. Under Bazel it would need a wasm32-unknown-unknown platform for rules_rust, a C toolchain whose clang targets wasm32 for bundled SQLite (rusqlite's sqlite-wasm-rs), crates/clax-worker's own Cargo.lock in crate_universe, worker-build (crates/clax-worker/build.sh installs it with cargo install) and wrangler from npm. Until then a local just ci does not run them; just check-wasm and just worker-test do.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"f75be890b6096e95cba144280fc77498d29f12bed337bdff3b9c0e486005b53e"},"summary":"Build crates/clax-worker and check the Worker's crates for wasm32 under Bazel","tags":["build","ci","revisit:rules_rust builds a wasm32 target with a C toolchain here, or a wasm32 break reaches main past the worker job","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
